# Silken Strength has flash: Bot1's Grizzly Bears attacked on turn 3 and is tapped on Bot2's turn 4. In the declare-attackers
# step Bot1 flashes the Aura onto it; "When this Aura enters, untap enchanted permanent" untaps it (CR 701.26a) and it is a
# 3/4 with reach, so it can block Bot2's Memnite and kill it, taking 1.

[Bot1 Deck]
Mox Emerald
Mox Jet
Grizzly Bears
Silken Strength
Swamp x16

[Bot2 Deck]
Memnite
Island x19

[Actions]
Bot1.Hand.Mox Emerald.Cast
Bot1.Hand.Mox Jet.Cast
Bot1.Battlefield.Mox Emerald.Activate
Bot1.Battlefield.Mox Jet.Activate
Bot1.Hand.Grizzly Bears.Cast
Bot1.Pass
Bot2.Pass
[T2 Bot2.Main1]
Bot2.Hand.Memnite.Cast
Bot2.Pass
Bot1.Pass
[T3 Bot1.DeclareAttackers]
Bot1.Attack(Grizzly Bears > Bot2)
[T3 Bot1.Main2]
? Bot1.Battlefield.Grizzly Bears.Tapped = true
[T4 Bot2.DeclareAttackers]
Bot2.Attack(Memnite > Bot1)
Bot1.Battlefield.Mox Emerald.Activate
Bot1.Battlefield.Mox Jet.Activate
Bot1.Hand.Silken Strength.Cast(Bot1.Battlefield.Grizzly Bears)
Bot1.Pass
Bot2.Pass
Bot1.Pass
Bot2.Pass
? Bot1.Battlefield.Grizzly Bears.Tapped = false
Bot1.Block(Grizzly Bears > Memnite)
[T4 Bot2.Main2]

[Expect]
Bot2.Graveyard = Memnite
Bot1.Life = 20
Bot2.Life = 18
Bot1.Battlefield.Grizzly Bears.Power = 3
Bot1.Battlefield.Grizzly Bears.Toughness = 4
Bot1.Battlefield.Grizzly Bears.Keywords = Reach
Bot1.Battlefield.Grizzly Bears.Damage = 1
